WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.060
Applied digital's $3.2 billion plan places 210 megawatts near Brookwood, Alabama. This is AI Chips &amp; Data Centres, Episode 4. Data

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:19.060
Centre Dynamics reports the project is announced under the name Delta Forge 2 in Tuscaloosa County. Operations are

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:28.640
expected to begin in 2028. The site covers 1,300 acres and 1.2 million square feet at full buildout. Applied

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.960
Digital says it will support up to 1,000 construction jobs and 100 permanent roles.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.020
The customer is described as an investment-grade hyperscaler.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.920
In June, that customer was already secured, and only now is the hall tied to this county.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.600
Community benefits committed to the Tuscaloosa County Economic Development Authority come

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:56.980
to $270 million over 20 years, plus an estimated $131 million in tax revenue.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:05.260
The contracted book is 5 AI factory campuses, 1.4 gigawatts of critical IT load, and about

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:09.040
2.15 gigawatts of grid-connected utility power.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:15.320
Micron's Jeremy Werner, who runs the Core Data Center Business Unit, says Agentec AI

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.940
uses two compute stacks, not one.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:22.920
The GPU reasons and plans, the CPU orchestrates the actions.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:29.000
positions. He points to KV Cash as what keeps context on hand. Larger contexts and

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.760
agentic jobs, he says, push memory demand well past reasoning by itself.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:41.940
Serve the home has a review up of the Azeroth Rack Soranod 8-2L2T. It is a new board for

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:48.580
AMD's Epic 80005, the Sorano line. The write-up calls out lots of connectivity for that

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:49.640
processor family.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:56.360
Frownhofer IAF has built a monolithic microwave integrated circuit aimed at modern data centers

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.740
plus measurement systems and sensors.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:04.920
Semiconductor Digest calls the part a broadband distributed amplifier and describes the

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.500
performance as outstanding.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:12.780
Vertiv has agreed to buy Ireland-based King Environmental Services, data center dynamics

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.260
reports.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:19.280
KES does fluid management, commissioning, and load testing for high-density liquid cooled

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:25.920
halls. The point of the deal is EMEA. Vertive already sells that fluid work in North America.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.900
Last year it bought purge right in the same line of work for more than $1 billion.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:38.420
Chief Executive GeoAlbertazi said that as density rises, cooling and power performance will depend

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:42.680
as much on execution in the field as on engineering and system design.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:52.100
KES started in 2002, sits near Dublin, covers EMEA, and its site shows work for Microsoft and Equinix.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:57.880
Data Center Knowledge reports that infrasound from data centers is drawing more scrutiny from nearby

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:03.900
communities. The argument there is that operators need mitigation upfront, and they need to say

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.240
plainly what they are doing.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:11.780
Semi-conductor digest reports ACCM is adding U.S. manufacturing across four advanced

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:15.820
material segments for AI infrastructure at a Wisconsin plant.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:21.580
Laminate output of 20 million square feet a year is scheduled to come online in January

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:22.640
2027.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:29.280
Buildup and prepreg, 87 million square feet a year, are scheduled for November 2026.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:35.640
Semi-conductor engineering's Weak &amp; Review says equipment and critical materials supply chains are tightening.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:43.320
The same review says TSMC's partners are accelerating, and that China is doubling down on AI compute and memory.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.680
You take it apart at the floor plate, not at the silicon.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:51.120
A hull slab carries a point load rating and a uniform load rating.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:59.260
The rack designer spends that allowance on bus bar, manifold, cold plates, and coolant until the frame is as heavy as the tile.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:02.660
will allow. The purchase order is not on that drawing.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:12.520
Dylan Patel puts a fully loaded GB300NVL72 at roughly 1,580 kg. He says recent purchase orders

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:21.020
price that rack at $5 million. The GB200NVL72 generation, in the same post, was $4 million.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:21.360
$8 million.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:29.740
A Vera Rubin NVL72, he adds, is already quoted as high as $8.8 million on essentially

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:30.620
that same mass.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.040
Four prices and weights, one chassis envelope.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:40.560
High bandwidth memory, the co-os package that joins it to the GPU, and the power stages

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.300
feeding both at little weight and most of the bill.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:49.680
His claim is that those three stay supply constrained, so value per kilogram climbs while

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:55.060
the floor holds the kilogram count still. What arrives on the dock is the populated frame,

00:04:55.580 --> 00:05:00.900
which is why he prices the rack rather than the bear packages. A higher quote does not buy

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:06.320
you a heavier legal frame, and a heavier frame would not clear a slab already at its rating.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:12.960
The trade-off flips when packaging allocation or feeder capacity, not steel, is the short resource.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:18.440
Price can move inside a fixed tile. The tile cannot grow to match the quote.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:24.420
On the horizon, Verdev expects the King Environmental Services deal to close before the end of

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:31.620
2026. Applied digital anticipates first operations in August 2027 at Polaris 4G3,

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:38.660
announced at 300 MW of critical IT load on 600 acres in an unnamed northern state.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:43.940
For the same US investment-graded hyperscaler previously signed for Delta 4G1.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:48.660
Before we go, the nearest date is that King Environmental Services close.

